<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Keeps the Mac awake so the scrape pipeline actually runs.

  Install:  cp deploy/selfhost/com.coreprop.caffeinate.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
            launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.coreprop.caffeinate.plist
  Stop:     launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.coreprop.caffeinate.plist
  Verify:   pmset -g assertions | grep -i preventsystemsleep

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  ---------------
  `pmset -g custom` reports `sleep 1` — this Mac suspends after one minute idle.
  A sleeping host does not scrape: on 2026-08-14 the pipeline logged a 439-minute
  gap (08:22 -> 15:41) that ended the instant the lid was opened, plus repeated
  25-90 minute gaps overnight. Users saw hours-old prop lines presented as
  current, which is worse than an honest outage.

  The permanent fix is `sudo pmset -a sleep 0`, which needs a password and so
  cannot be automated here. This is the no-sudo equivalent.

  FLAGS
  -----
    -i  prevent idle system sleep
    -m  prevent disk from idle-sleeping
    -s  prevent system sleep  (ONLY asserted while on AC power)
    -u  declare user activity, so the idle timer keeps resetting

  A bare `caffeinate -i` was already running and was NOT sufficient — the sleep
  log shows "Entering Sleep state due to 'Maintenance Sleep'" at 14:07, 14:12
  and 14:31 with that assertion held. `-s` is the one that covers those.

  Display sleep is deliberately NOT prevented (no -d): the screen may still turn
  off, which saves power and does not affect the scraper.

  *** LIMITATION — READ THIS ***
  caffeinate CANNOT prevent clamshell (lid-close) sleep on a MacBook. If the lid
  is shut without an external display + power, the machine sleeps regardless and
  scraping stops. The 439-minute gap above was a lid-close event. Options:
    - keep the lid open, or
    - run the Mac in clamshell mode on AC with an external display, or
    - `sudo pmset -b disablesleep 1` (needs a password; disables lid sleep).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.coreprop.caffeinate</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/caffeinate</string>
        <string>-i</string>
        <string>-m</string>
        <string>-s</string>
        <string>-u</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- caffeinate holds the assertion for as long as it runs, so if it ever
         dies the machine becomes sleepable again. Restart it unconditionally. -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/seniortech/Library/Logs/coreprop/caffeinate.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/seniortech/Library/Logs/coreprop/caffeinate.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
